        <article class="mt-4">
          <p class="lead">The <strong>Chess Wizards Quiz</strong>, held across <strong>Hippocampus Learning Centres (HLC)</strong> to celebrate <strong>International Chess Day</strong>, blended the timeless strategy of chess with the excitement of technology-driven learning. 
          Conducted on <strong>Kahoot</strong>, a globally popular game-based learning platform, the event turned classrooms into live digital arenas where students tested their chess knowledge, raced against time, and cheered as leaderboards shifted in real time. This initiative perfectly reflected HLC’s mission of delivering interactive, <strong>21st-century education</strong>—combining fun, learning, and technological engagement.</p>

          <h2 id="section1">Introduction: Where Strategy Meets Technology</h2>
          <p>At Hippocampus, learning is more than just lessons—it’s an experience that excites, challenges, and inspires. 
          This year, on International Chess Day, students got to explore the strategic world of chess in a way they had never before imagined.</p>
          
          <p>The Chess Wizards Quiz turned traditional learning into an electrifying digital adventure. 
          Combining the intellectual thrill of chess with Kahoot’s real-time quizzes, the competition encouraged quick thinking, teamwork, and a spirit of healthy rivalry.</p>
          
          <blockquote>“It’s so much fun to see kids excited to show their talent in a unique chess game conducted by the team. We should also participate in such activities,” said Roopashree, R&D Program Manager at Hippocampus.</blockquote>


          <h2 id="section2">The Competition: Fun, Fair, and Fierce</h2>
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px;">Stage 1: The Intra-School Challenge</h3>

          <p>The first stage of the competition brought together students from individual schools for an adrenaline-filled contest. 
          Each student competed against peers within their own campus, solving rapid-fire chess-related questions. 
          The atmosphere was filled with cheers, thoughtful silence, and friendly rivalry.</p>

          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px;">Stage 2: The Inter-School Showdown</h3>

          <p>Top scorers from Stage 1 advanced to the inter-school finale, where the stakes were higher, and the challenge tougher. 
          Students from multiple Hippocampus schools joined virtually through Kahoot, turning the competition into a large-scale event of excitement and strategy. 
          The thrill of competing against peers beyond their classroom pushed students to aim higher and think faster.</p>

          <h2 id="section3">Teachers and Technology: The Pillars Behind the Magic</h2>
          <p>None of this would have been possible without the dedicated teachers and staff who powered the event behind the scenes. 
          They mastered Kahoot’s digital interface, facilitated real-time coordination, and ensured every student had an equal opportunity to shine.</p>
          
          <p>Through video conferencing, live commentary, and projected leaderboards, the quiz was elevated from a classroom activity to a schoolwide celebration of learning and technology.</p>

          <p>As Pooja Ramchandani, School Correspondent at Hippocampus, observed: </p>
          <blockquote>“They all had fun. There was a lot of excitement and shouts, especially by the end of it when they won.”</blockquote>


          <h2 id="section4">The Real-Time Thrill: Learning Comes Alive</h2>

          <p>The most captivating aspect of the Chess Wizards Quiz was the real-time competition experience. 
          With Kahoot’s interactive format, students saw their scores surge or drop instantly on live leaderboards. 
          Each correct answer nudged them closer to victory, while every near miss spurred determination.</p>
          
          <p>The dynamic pace of the quiz transformed classrooms into virtual arenas of strategic thinking, where quick reasoning met technological fluency.</p>
          

