          <h2 id="section5">Recognizing Chess Champions: The Winning Minds</h2>
          <p>To honor the students’ passion and hard work, cash prizes were awarded to the top performers in both junior and senior categories.</p>
          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px;">Senior Category (Grades 8–10)</h3>
          <ul>
          <li>1st Prize – Abhishek, Class 10, Sri Siddaroodha Public School – ₹1500</li>
          <li>2nd Prize – Tejas C., Class 9, Vidya Vaibhav Hippocampus Public School – ₹750</li>
          <li>3rd Prize – Laalithya C.S., Class 8, Malnad Hippocampus School – ₹350</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 style="font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 15px;">Junior Category (Grades 5–7)</h3>
          <ul>
          <li>1st Prize – Rakshit Patil, Class 6, Sri Siddaroodha Public School – ₹1500</li>
          <li>2nd Prize – Dimple, Class 6, SSVM Hippocampus School – ₹750</li>
          <li>3rd Prize – Srusti, Class 7, SSVM Hippocampus School – ₹350</li>
          </ul>

          <p>These bright achievers not only excelled in chess knowledge but also embodied the spirit of <strong>focus, logic, and critical thinking</strong>—the very traits that chess teaches so well.</p>


          <h2 id="section6">A Futuristic Learning Experience</h2>
          <p>The <strong>Chess Wizards Quiz</strong> exemplified Hippocampus’s mission of <strong>combining education with innovation</strong>. 
          By merging chess—a centuries-old strategy game—with digital tools like <strong>Kahoot</strong>, the event created an engaging bridge between tradition and modernity.</p>
          
          <p>Students developed:</p>
          <ul>
          <li><strong>Analytical and strategic thinking</strong> through chess challenges</li>
          <li><strong>Digital literacy</strong> by engaging with game-based technology</li>
          <li><strong>Collaboration and communication</strong> through teamwork and peer interaction</li>
          </ul>

          <p>The lively blend of <strong>technology, competition, and joy</strong> made this event not just a quiz but a milestone in <strong>experiential learning</strong> at HLC.</p>

          <h2 id="section6">Conclusion: The Checkmate of Education and Innovation</h2>
          <p>The <strong>Kahoot Chess Wizards Quiz</strong> was more than an event—it was a celebration of innovation in education. 
          It proved that learning can be thrilling, technology can be empowering, and classrooms can transform into digital stages for discovery.</p>
          <p>At Hippocampus, we continue to redefine education by merging <strong>fun, technology, and holistic learning</strong>. 
          With every quiz, challenge, and event, we bring students closer to a future where knowledge is not memorized but <strong>experienced</strong>.</p>
          
          <p>The game may end with a checkmate, but at Hippocampus, the learning never stops.<p>


